==French==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|fr|frm|suyvre}}, from {{inh|fr|fro|sivre}}, {{m|fro|siure}}, {{m|fro|segre}}, from {{inh|fr|VL.||*sequere}} of deponent {{inh|fr|la|sequor|sequī}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA}}
* {{audio|fr|Fr-suivre.ogg|audio}}
* {{IPA|fr|[sɥiv(r)]|[sɥir]|[swir]|a=Louisiana}}

===Verb===
{{fr-verb}}

# to [[follow]] (literal sense)
#: {{ux|fr|Je t'invite à me '''suivre.'''|I invite you '''to follow''' me.}}
# to [[follow]]; to [[get]] (figurative sense; to understand what someone is saying)
#: {{ux|fr|Il nous faut travailler dur. Tu me '''suis''' ?|We have to work hard. '''Do''' you '''get''' me?}}
# to [[take]] (a course or a class)
#: {{ux|fr|Ma sœur '''suit''' un cours d'italien.|My sister '''is taking''' an Italian course.}}

